---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Software for multi-location pottery studios"
	description="Kilnbook for pottery studios with more than one location: multiple locations with one member account, unlimited kilns, staff roles and shift notes."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Multi-location studios</p>
				<h1>More than one studio, one member account.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					The Collective plan covers multiple locations with one member account, unlimited kilns, and
					staff roles and shift notes so each shift knows what the last one did.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="A studio floor plan with six wheels, a kiln room, drying shelves and a glaze table"
				width="560"
				height="360"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>What changes when you open a second studio</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Which studio is my piece at?"</h3>
					<p>
						Members throw at more than one location and do not want a separate sign-up at each
						studio.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Nobody told me the kiln was loaded."</h3>
					<p>
						Different staff open and close each location, and handover happens in a group chat if it
						happens at all.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Every studio does it differently."</h3>
					<p>
						Each location ends up with its own spreadsheet, its own kiln log and its own way of taking
						payment.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Built for studios with more than one floor</h2>
		<p>
			Once you run two or more locations, the hard part is keeping them consistent. With Kilnbook,
			every location uses the same firing queues, class booking and wheel calendars.
		</p>

		<h2>One account per member</h2>
		<p>
			On the Collective plan, all of your locations sit under one Kilnbook account, and each member
			has a single member account rather than a separate sign-up at every studio.
		</p>

		<h2>Firing queues for every kiln</h2>
		<p>
			Each kiln has its own queue for bisque and glaze firings, with fees charged by cubic inch and a
			pickup text when the load comes out. The Collective plan has no limit on kilns.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Staff roles and shift notes</h2>
		<p>
			Staff roles give front-desk staff the access their job needs, and instructors get their own
			login with today's roster. Shift notes let the person closing tell the person opening what is
			in the kiln and what still needs doing.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes and wheel time at each site</h2>
		<p>
			Run courses, drop-ins and class packs with waitlists that fill themselves, and let members
			reserve wheels and tables in one-hour blocks.
			<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a> ·
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel time</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>The Collective plan</h2>
		<p>
			Multiple locations, unlimited kilns, staff roles and priority support from a real potter, for
			$149 a month. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="band-dark quote-band">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<blockquote class="quote">
				[Quote from the owner of a multi-location studio about running every site on Kilnbook]
				<cite>[Name, role, studio (city)]</cite>
			</blockquote>
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Proof</p>
				<h2>Trusted by studios in three countries</h2>
				<p>
					Over 340 studios in the US, Canada and the UK run their bookings, firings and memberships on
					Kilnbook.
				</p>
				<p>[Result a multi-location studio saw after switching to Kilnbook, with a number]</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Run every studio from one front desk.</h2>
			<p>30 days free to start. No card needed, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
